    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d563">

                <pb facs="0774" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg668"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Reid to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-01-31"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 31, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 134.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to Mr. Carter’s dispatch of
                    the 29th ultimo<anchor n="a" xml:id="d563-f1"/> on the subject of the
                    Newfoundland fisheries question, I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy of
                    a report of Inspector O’Reilly to the minister of justice in Newfoundland, dated
                    the 21st ultimo, which has been sent to me by Sir Edward Grey, confirming and
                    extending the report already communicated in the dispatch above mentioned, and
                    is to the effect that the complaint of malicious damage to American fishing nets
                    and fishing tackle by the Newfoundland fishermen was unfounded.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitelaw Reid.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d563-a1.xml" xpointer="d563-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
